      "text": "Opera is the union of music and drama in which the text is (usually entirely) sung. It is simultaneously a musical form, a theatrical form, and a social institution. Its 400-year history reflects successive attempts to balance the demands of music and drama — a tension that has never been finally resolved."
    },
    {
