        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Opera",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nOPERA SERIA (\"serious opera\")\n------------------------------\nThe dominant form, ~1650–1780.\nTexts: mythology, ancient history.\nStructure: recitative (speech-like) + aria (song)."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-OPERA.md#013",
      "path": [
        "07-OPERA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:theater-performance:07-opera, git-history:theater-performance:07-opera]",
        "canonical_path": "theater-performance/07-OPERA.md",
        "concepts": "[opera]",
        "current_path": "theater-performance/07-OPERA.md",
        "id": "maxim:theater-performance:opera",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "theater-performance",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[opera]",
        "section": "theater-performance",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Opera",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "RECITATIVE:\n  Sung speech; the text is clear; the action advances.\n  Two types:\n    Secco (\"dry\"): voice + harpsichord only.\n      Fast, efficient text delivery.\n    Accompagnato (\"accompanied\"): full orchestra.\n      For more emotionally charged passages."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-OPERA.md#014",
      "path": [
        "07-OPERA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:theater-performance:07-opera, git-history:theater-performance:07-opera]",
        "canonical_path": "theater-performance/07-OPERA.md",
        "concepts": "[opera]",
        "current_path": "theater-performance/07-OPERA.md",
        "id": "maxim:theater-performance:opera",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "theater-performance",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[opera]",
        "section": "theater-performance",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Opera",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "ARIA:\n  A formal song; the action pauses while a character\n  sings of their emotional state.\n  DA CAPO ARIA (A-B-A' form):\n    A: main material\n    B: contrasting section\n    A': return, with improvised ornamentation\n    The singer added ornamentation on the DA CAPO.\n    The score was a skeleton; the singer completed it.\n    This is the opposite of later practice (full notation)."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-OPERA.md#015",
      "path": [
        "07-OPERA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:theater-performance:07-opera, git-history:theater-performance:07-opera]",
        "canonical_path": "theater-performance/07-OPERA.md",
        "concepts": "[opera]",
        "current_path": "theater-performance/07-OPERA.md",
        "id": "maxim:theater-performance:opera",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "theater-performance",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[opera]",
        "section": "theater-performance",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Opera",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "OPERA SERIA CONVENTIONS:\n  3 acts; each character gets one aria per act.\n  No ensembles (duets/trios etc.) of consequence — arias\n  only. This is dramatically rigid but musically splendid.\n  The castrato (castrated male soprano) was the vocal\n  ideal — superhuman power and range.\n  Handel wrote many of his best roles for castrato."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-OPERA.md#016",
      "path": [
        "07-OPERA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:theater-performance:07-opera, git-history:theater-performance:07-opera]",
        "canonical_path": "theater-performance/07-OPERA.md",
        "concepts": "[opera]",
        "current_path": "theater-performance/07-OPERA.md",
        "id": "maxim:theater-performance:opera",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "theater-performance",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[opera]",
        "section": "theater-performance",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Opera",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "OPERA BUFFA (\"comic opera\")\n----------------------------\nLower-class characters; contemporary settings;\nsocial satire; ensemble finales (the \"chain finale\"\nthat ends each act — all characters onstage, multiple\ntempos and keys)."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-OPERA.md#017",
      "path": [
        "07-OPERA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:theater-performance:07-opera, git-history:theater-performance:07-opera]",
