      "text": "### Gluck: The Drama Must Win"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-OPERA.md#021",
      "path": [
        "07-OPERA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:theater-performance:07-opera, git-history:theater-performance:07-opera]",
        "canonical_path": "theater-performance/07-OPERA.md",
        "concepts": "[opera]",
        "current_path": "theater-performance/07-OPERA.md",
        "id": "maxim:theater-performance:opera",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "theater-performance",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[opera]",
        "section": "theater-performance",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Opera",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Christoph Willibald Gluck's \"reform operas\" (Orfeo ed Euridice, 1762; Alceste, 1767) attempted to subordinate music to drama:"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-OPERA.md#022",
      "path": [
        "07-OPERA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:theater-performance:07-opera, git-history:theater-performance:07-opera]",
        "canonical_path": "theater-performance/07-OPERA.md",
        "concepts": "[opera]",
        "current_path": "theater-performance/07-OPERA.md",
        "id": "maxim:theater-performance:opera",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "theater-performance",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[opera]",
        "section": "theater-performance",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Opera",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nGLUCK'S REFORM MANIFESTO (Alceste preface, 1769)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\"I sought to restrict music to its true office of\nserving poetry by means of expression... by a\nbeautiful simplicity; not wishing, for this purpose,\nto pass over unnaturally the second [A'] part of an\naria where the text allows no variation of meaning.\""
    },
    {
      "id": "07-OPERA.md#023",
      "path": [
        "07-OPERA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:theater-performance:07-opera, git-history:theater-performance:07-opera]",
        "canonical_path": "theater-performance/07-OPERA.md",
        "concepts": "[opera]",
        "current_path": "theater-performance/07-OPERA.md",
        "id": "maxim:theater-performance:opera",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "theater-performance",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[opera]",
        "section": "theater-performance",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Opera",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Against: da capo aria's ornamentation.\nAgainst: the castrato's vocal display for its own sake.\nAgainst: the halt of drama for the aria."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-OPERA.md#024",
      "path": [
        "07-OPERA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:theater-performance:07-opera, git-history:theater-performance:07-opera]",
        "canonical_path": "theater-performance/07-OPERA.md",
        "concepts": "[opera]",
        "current_path": "theater-performance/07-OPERA.md",
        "id": "maxim:theater-performance:opera",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "theater-performance",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[opera]",
        "section": "theater-performance",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Opera",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "FOR: continuous musical drama; the music serves the text."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-OPERA.md#025",
      "path": [
        "07-OPERA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:theater-performance:07-opera, git-history:theater-performance:07-opera]",
        "canonical_path": "theater-performance/07-OPERA.md",
