        "module": "theater-performance",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[opera]",
        "section": "theater-performance",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Opera",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "This is the Camerata's original ideal restated.\nBut now as a reaction against what Baroque opera had become."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-OPERA.md#026",
      "path": [
        "07-OPERA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:theater-performance:07-opera, git-history:theater-performance:07-opera]",
        "canonical_path": "theater-performance/07-OPERA.md",
        "concepts": "[opera]",
        "current_path": "theater-performance/07-OPERA.md",
        "id": "maxim:theater-performance:opera",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "theater-performance",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[opera]",
        "section": "theater-performance",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Opera",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The reform cycle: opera keeps oscillating between\nmusic-dominant (singer's vehicle, vocal display) and\ndrama-dominant (the music serves the text/scene).\nGluck: drama dominant.\nRossini (bel canto): music/voice dominant.\nWagner: attempts a synthesis but creates a new extreme.\nVerdi: gradually moves toward drama.\n20th c.: various solutions.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-OPERA.md#027",
      "path": [
